<!-- ── §1 MEETING DETAILS ─────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="chapter">
  <div class="chapter-head">
    <span class="chapter-n">§1</span>
    <span class="chapter-title">Meeting Details</span>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>Italy Nihao Group Limited</strong><br>
      (Incorporated in Hong Kong SAR)<br>
      Company Registration No.: [________]
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>RESOLUTIONS OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS</strong><br>
      Passed at a duly convened meeting held on [________] 2026<br><br>
      <strong>Re:</strong> Authorisation of Cross-Border Carbon Credit Trading,
      Custody Services, and CEA-EUA Conversion Operations
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── §2 PRESENT ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="chapter">
  <div class="chapter-head">
    <span class="chapter-n">§2</span>
    <span class="chapter-title">Present</span>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="highlight-line">
      <div class="highlight-label">Directors in Attendance</div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
          <td>Name</td>
          <td><strong>Title</strong></td>
          <td><strong>Capacity</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>[Director Name 1]</td>
          <td><strong>Managing Director</strong></td>
          <td>Chairman</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>[Director Name 2]</td>
          <td><strong>Director</strong></td>
          <td>Director</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>[Director Name 3]</td>
          <td><strong>Director</strong></td>
          <td>Director</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-body">
      The Chairman confirmed that a quorum was present and declared the meeting duly constituted.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-body">
      The Chairman reported that the purpose of the meeting was to consider and, if thought fit,
      to approve the commencement and continuation of the Company's cross-border carbon credit
      trading, custody, conversion, and related activities, and to authorise the necessary
      operational, compliance, and contractual arrangements.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── §3 BACKGROUND ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="chapter">
  <div class="chapter-head">
    <span class="chapter-n">§3</span>
    <span class="chapter-title">Background</span>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-body">
      The Board noted the following:
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">3.1</span>
      <span class="article-title">Commercial Background</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      The Company has been engaged in cross-border commercial activities between Europe and the
      People's Republic of China for an extended period, and has developed expertise and
      operational infrastructure spanning both markets.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">3.2</span>
      <span class="article-title">Commercial Opportunity</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      The Company has identified a commercial opportunity in facilitating the bilateral trading,
      custody, and cross-border conversion of carbon credits, specifically EU Allowances (EUA)
      traded under the EU Emissions Trading System and Chinese Emission Allowances (CEA) traded
      under the PRC pilot and national emissions trading schemes.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">3.3</span>
      <span class="article-title">Principal Counterparty Model</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      The Company proposes to operate as a principal counterparty in carbon credit transactions,
      holding legal title to carbon credits and providing clients with beneficial ownership rights,
      rather than acting as broker, agent, or intermediary.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">3.4</span>
      <span class="article-title">Regulatory Position</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      The Company's legal advisers have confirmed that, under the current laws of Hong Kong SAR,
      carbon credits are not classified as securities, futures contracts, or regulated investment
      products within the meaning of the applicable securities and futures legislation in Hong Kong,
      and that no dedicated licence is required for bilateral OTC trading in carbon credits between
      institutional counterparties.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">3.5</span>
      <span class="article-title">Compliance Framework</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      The Company's Compliance Officer has prepared a Regulatory Position Memorandum
      (Ref: NIHA-RPM-2026-001) confirming the regulatory position and recommending voluntary
      adoption of compliance standards aligned with applicable anti-money laundering legislation,
      FATF Recommendations, and the applicable regulatory authority best practice guidelines.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">3.6</span>
      <span class="article-title">Registry Accounts</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      The Company has obtained SAFE-approved foreign investor registration at the China Emissions
      Exchange (Shenzhen) (CEEX) and maintains operational accounts at relevant European carbon
      registries.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── §4 RESOLUTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="chapter">
  <div class="chapter-head">
    <span class="chapter-n">§4</span>
    <span class="chapter-title">Resolutions</span>
  </div>
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-body">
      After due consideration and discussion, the following resolutions were unanimously passed:
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 1 — Principal Trading Authorisation -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.1</span>
      <span class="article-title">Principal Trading Authorisation</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>RESOLVED,</strong> that the Company is hereby authorised to engage in cross-border
      carbon credit trading, custody, conversion, and related services as a principal counterparty,
      including but not limited to the acquisition, holding, transfer, conversion, and retirement
      of EU Allowances (EUA), Chinese Emission Allowances (CEA), and voluntary carbon credits
      (VCU) on behalf of itself and its clients.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 2 — Document Approval -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.2</span>
      <span class="article-title">Document Approval</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that the following documents, copies of which have been
      tabled at this meeting and initialled by the Chairman for identification, are hereby approved
      and adopted:
      <div class="highlight-line" style="margin-top: 12px;">
        <table class="data-table">
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-CCA-2026-001</td>
            <td>Carbon Credit Custody Agreement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-MSA-2026-001</td>
            <td>Master Service Agreement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-NDA-2026-001</td>
            <td>Non-Disclosure Agreement template</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-RDS-2026-001</td>
            <td>Risk Disclosure Statement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-OBD-2026-001</td>
            <td>Client Onboarding and KYC Application Pack</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-TEP-2026-001</td>
            <td>Trade Execution Policy</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-CPM-2026-001</td>
            <td>Compliance Policy Manual</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-BCP-2026-001</td>
            <td>Business Continuity Plan</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Ref: NIHA-RPM-2026-001</td>
            <td>Regulatory Position Memorandum</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 3 — Compliance Officer Appointment -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.3</span>
      <span class="article-title">Compliance Officer Appointment</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that [Director Name / Compliance Officer] is hereby
      appointed as the designated Compliance Officer of the Company for the purposes of the
      applicable anti-money laundering and counter-terrorist financing legislation in Hong Kong
      and all related compliance functions, with authority to implement and enforce the Compliance
      Policy Manual.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 4 — Segregated Client Accounts -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.4</span>
      <span class="article-title">Segregated Client Accounts</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that the Company shall maintain segregated client accounts
      for both funds and carbon credits, separate from the Company's proprietary assets, in
      accordance with the Custody Agreement and applicable best practice standards.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 5 — Authorised Signatories -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.5</span>
      <span class="article-title">Authorised Signatories</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that [Managing Director Name] and [Director Name 2],
      acting jointly, are hereby authorised to:
      <div class="highlight-line" style="margin-top: 12px;">
        <div class="highlight-body">
          (a) open and operate bank accounts, registry accounts, and trading platform accounts
          as required for the carbon credit business;<br><br>
          (b) execute the approved contractual documents on behalf of the Company with clients
          and counterparties;<br><br>
          (c) engage external legal counsel, auditors, and compliance consultants as necessary;<br><br>
          (d) represent the Company in dealings with regulatory authorities, exchanges, and
          industry bodies;<br><br>
          (e) approve individual client onboarding applications following satisfactory completion
          of KYC and due diligence procedures.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 6 — Working Capital Allocation -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.6</span>
      <span class="article-title">Working Capital Allocation</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that the Company shall allocate initial working capital
      of [HKD / EUR ________] to the carbon credit trading business, subject to review and
      adjustment by the Board on a quarterly basis.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 7 — Quarterly Compliance Reporting -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.7</span>
      <span class="article-title">Quarterly Compliance Reporting</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that the Compliance Officer shall present a quarterly
      compliance report to the Board, including transaction volumes, risk assessments, regulatory
      developments, and any reportable incidents.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Resolution 8 — General Authority -->
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-head">
      <span class="article-n">R.8</span>
      <span class="article-title">General Authority</span>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body">
      <strong>FURTHER RESOLVED,</strong> that any director of the Company is authorised to do
      all such acts and things and to sign, execute, and deliver all such documents and instruments
      as may be necessary or desirable to give effect to these resolutions.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

